# ARM's EGL config table, read by libGLES_mali r38p1 in EVERY process that
# touches EGL. Set in configs/properties/vendor.prop; see the long note there
# for what they are and why the values are what they are.
#
# This line is HALF THE FIX and the half that is easy to miss. Unlabelled,
# ro.vendor.arm.* falls through to vendor_default_prop, and no app domain can
# read that — so the properties are set correctly, present in getprop, visible
# to root, and INVISIBLE to the app that needs them. The driver then sees them
# as unset and rebuilds the broken config table. Measured 2026-08-27: with the
# values set and this label missing, WhatsApp's camera still force-closed and
# logged, 100 times per property:
#
#   W libc: Access denied finding property
#           "ro.vendor.arm.egl.configs.r8_g8_b8_a8_32bit_fixed.recordable"
#
# vendor_mtk_gpu_prop is the right type and needs no new grant: it is declared
# by device/mediatek/sepolicy_vndr (basic/non_plat/property.te:107) and carries
# mtk_core_property_type, and basic/non_plat/domain.te:8 has
# get_prop(domain, mtk_core_property_type) — so every domain, apps included,
# can read it. That grant is ATTRIBUTE-mediated, so it is invisible to a grep
# for the type name (BLUEPRINT §9). vendor_restricted_prop restricts only
# WRITING, which init does from /vendor/build.prop.
#
# ro.vendor.arm. rather than ro.vendor.arm.egl.configs. — the same prefix
# Samsung uses on the same SoC, and it also covers the ro.vendor.arm.gralloc.*
# keys the driver reads. Verified against the shipped contexts and MediaTek's:
# nothing else claims this prefix, so there is no conflicting type to capture.
#
# 🔴 This class CANNOT be live-tested on this device — property_contexts is
# read before post-fs-data, where KSU mounts (RESUME §"the method that
# worked"). It was proven instead by granting the read directly under
# Enforcing (ksud sepolicy patch, allow appdomain vendor_default_prop) and
# re-testing: crash 1 -> 0, force-finish 2 -> 0, capture completing through to
# MediaComposerActivity. The label must still be confirmed in a BUILD.
ro.vendor.arm.                              u:object_r:vendor_mtk_gpu_prop:s0
